work_schedule:
  thesis: >-
    Submit one format-table kernel and finish its device synchronization
    before the five-kernel MoE pipeline, executed eagerly or by graph replay.
    The tables are global module state with no consumer in this pipeline.
    One CTA prepares all routing metadata using shared group
    histograms and prefixes, replacing separate count, scan and scatter grids
    and their device memset. Flat gather exposes broad parallelism;
    statically strided persistent GEMM workers amortize setup and retain rings across
    expert tiles. PDL grants early launch, while consumers still wait for predecessor
    completion before reading its results.
    Global workspace persists across requests and graph replays; its R-row packed
    operand and route-result views retain unwritten bytes. Same-stream ordering
    orders their reuse. After the initialization prefix this path adds no
    cross-stream workspace exclusion or host wait for final output completion.
  flow:
    launch:
      - {phase: [init_tables]}
      - {phase: [prepare], protocol: pdl, start_after: init_tables.kernel_done}
      - {phase: [gather], protocol: pdl, start_after: prepare.launch_ready}
      - {phase: [fc1], protocol: pdl, start_after: gather.launch_ready}
      - {phase: [fc2], protocol: pdl, start_after: fc1.launch_ready}
      - {phase: [finalize], protocol: pdl, start_after: fc2.launch_ready}

